      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why mask here and in the set_read_idx?  You can just let the index increase and it will overflow at the natural word (uint16_t in this case) boundary.  Since the size of the FIFO is restricted to powers of two there is no issue when it wraps.  It also greatly simplifies things below.",
      "revId": "c0470bb514fabe7a488f10e2f1521e42149d0a19",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
